  m_Name: Cheesy Beet Bread
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::IngredientData
  _name: Cheesy Beet Bread
  _spoilTime: 15
  _normalSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 439333845acf64be7b41fe2f26ea6bc2, type: 3}
  _spoiledSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 56ad321ab177641f9a0feb9ce63558ef, type: 3}
  _plateSprite: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 92e1392c763c0417ca4a9d8f32ac89c1, type: 3}
  _isSmallIngredient: 0
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: "Some time ago, when the heavens thundered and
    the skies wept, a trader from the West came and asked for cheesy bread and a
    red soup in broken Aijin. A tired and overworked chef had the unfortunate opportunity
    to serve this strange man and his even stranger demands.  Spurred on by the man\u2019s
    patterings in childish Aijin, the chef threw together this recipe from what he
    had on hand. The trader cried out \"soup good!\" and \"feel best I!\"in between
    big chomps of hot bread drenched in thick soup, and left into the stormy night
    to who knows where. This recipe became a hit amongst the chef\u2019s customers
    after she recreated it for days to come, especially the children waiting out
    the stinging smog rains on their way home from a shift."
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: Once a comforting dish for young children, this
    spoiled soup now has a sour tang that runs alongside a reminiscent sweetness,
    featuring an intoxicating bite only comparable to strong vodka. The majority
    of kids despise this variation, but some cannot afford to pass on it. Others
    prefer it, though, as nothing comparable can make you forget the sight of your
    friends who end up on the wrong end of heavy machinery.
